   q: "A right of way has not been used for 60 years, because the dominant owners used a more convenient route. The servient owner says the easement has ended. Is that right?",
   o: ["Yes, because 20 years' non-use extinguishes an easement", "Yes, because using another route is an express release", "No, because an easement can end only by statute", "No, because non-use alone, especially where there was an alternative route, does not show an intention to abandon it permanently"],
